## Code
- three.js r170 (MIT), with EffectComposer, RenderPass, UnrealBloomPass, ShaderPass and ConvexGeometry from its examples,
  loaded from the library's node_modules.

## Images, models
- None. The terrain, the telescope, the sky, the clouds, the rain, the lunar module, the Earth and Moon, the control room
  and the TV picture are built or drawn in code; no photographs, no footage, no external models, no AI-generated images.
- The lunar module and the telescope are our own simplified models built from the vehicles' published general shape.
  The TV picture (a moonwalker by the lander) is our own drawing, not a frame of the 1969 broadcast.

## Facts
- Every date, time, number and event on screen and in the voice is sourced in demo/FACTS.md, with URLs and quoted wording.
